what do you think will be the most  effective way  to deter vladimir putin  from an invasion of ukraine  vladimir putin is first and foremost a  kleptocrat  he's been in power as a dictator for 20  years he's stolen an enormous amount of  money from the russian state um from  russian oligarchs from from others in  russia  and that money he doesn't keep in his  own name he keeps in the name of  trustees i call them oligarch trustees  and those oligarch trustees don't keep  that money in russia they keep that  money in the west and as you mentioned  we see it in london we see it in new  york we see it in south of france and  putin values that money more than human  life he's killed a lot of people to get  that money  and so in in in my mind the the cleanest  safest and simplest way of deterring  vladimir putin from invading ukraine is  to go after his money and there's a  piece of legislation in place it's  called the magnitsky act it was named  after my  lawyer who was killed in russia sergey  manninsky and it allows the british  government  to freeze the assets and ban the visas  of people who are involved in high-level  corruption and human rights abuse  and so we have a tool the magnitsky act  we actually know who these oligarchs are  and hold putin's assets um we know that  they are held in in london and we know  that putin values his money and so the  easy way of doing things for us  and in a very asymmetric way as far as  putin is concerned is to freeze the  money of a certain number of oligarchs  and i would argue that we should do so  before he invades ukraine to show that  he were serious instead of waiting for  him to actually cross the border  do you think um  that  some of this has been done  already or is is your case is your  concern  that um the money is too important  to the uk you know the property the  investments and so on for us to really  do this seriously  well it's it's an interesting question  because on one hand um i would i would  i've seen and i think everyone else has  seen that um we've been pretty soft on  russia here in the uk  in the past they've committed  terrible atrocities using novichok and  salisbury and polonium in london  the russians have been  sending  jets over our uh you know military jets  in in the  uh over our airspace they've been doing  all sorts of terrible things um and we  haven't done much and and the reason we  haven't done much in the past is because  um of all this russian money sloshing  around and a lot of people close to the  center of power benefiting from it but  and this is a really important but um  we're now in a new world where where  russia is is threatening the stability  of peace in europe  and um and because all that money is  still sloshing around here it gives us  what i would call an enormous amount of  leverage we're actually we could  potentially punch way above our weight  because all that money is here and if we  started to freeze it and seize it i  guarantee you putin would pay attention  yeah but of course the the other way of  looking at this is there's all this  money sloshing around there are a lot of  people here benefiting from it and i  don't just mean you know um fat cats in  the city but i mean for example people  who might benefit from investment of  that cash  freezing and seizing the oligarchs money  is not  a pain-free process for britain is it  well well i i would argue that that is  is very pain free in the sense that that  they can't there's no there's no  reciprocal measure that they can take  against us so it's not as if we have all  of our money in russia they have all of  their money here and they could  reciprocate um this is something that we  can be done asymmetrical so and so we  can do it and there's no way that they  can retaliate against that and so yes  there are people um in in the city of  london and people in the house of lords  and and other places who are  beneficiaries of this money but the but  their interests  these 